# A user turn is a bubble that hugs its own text, pushed flush to the right
# edge of the reading column, with its avatar beside it.
#
# Puffin's reference frame opens on exactly this shape and hanabi's transcript
# is measured against it, so the shape is worth pinning: three separate things
# have to hold at once and any one of them can rot on its own.
#
#   1. RIGHT-ALIGNED. The bubble's right edge is the column's right edge:
#      646 + 412 == 322 + 736 == 1058. This is the whole of what
#      JustifyContent::FlexEnd buys — there is no spacer sibling holding the
#      bubble over, so if the justification is lost the bubble slides left to
#      348 (the column, plus the avatar and its gap) and every number below
#      moves at once.
#   2. SHRINK-TO-FIT, CAPPED. 412 is this message's own wrapped width, not the
#      column's. A bubble that stopped hugging its text would be 644 (the cap,
#      kBubbleCap) or 736 (the column). afterhours cannot express "as wide as
#      my text but no wider than N" — see afterhours_gaps.md #87 — so this
#      width is computed by hanabi in user_box() and handed to the layout as a
#      literal pixels(). That makes it exactly the kind of number that rots
#      silently, and exactly the kind worth asserting.
#   3. TOP-ALIGNED, NOT CENTRED. The avatar's y is the bubble's y plus 6, on a
#      35px-tall bubble: it sits beside the FIRST line rather than floating
#      halfway down. Centred, it would be at 138 here and wrong the moment the
#      message wraps to two lines.
#
# Every figure was read out of the layout at this window size (assert_ui
# reports the actual when it fails, so a deliberate mismatch prints them), not
# derived from the constants — the point is to catch the constants and the
# layout disagreeing.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}

require_thread t2

expect_text "Reconcile this cycle's Stars payouts"

# The reading column the turn is laid out in.
assert_ui user_row x=322 w=736

# Flush right, and narrower than the column.
assert_ui user_bubble x=646 w=412 h=35

# Beside the bubble, 6px clear of it and 6px down from its top.
# The two y's moved 4px down with the transcript's top inset (8 -> 12, which is
# Puffin's own `EdgeInsets(top: 12, ...)`) on feat/vis-fixture; the 6px
# relationship between them is what this pair is actually asserting and it is
# unchanged.
assert_ui user_avatar x=620 y=141 w=20 h=20
assert_ui user_bubble y=135
